      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Why does HNSW consume 3.3x more RAM than IVFFlat in pgvector?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "HNSW constructs a multi-layer hierarchical proximity graph where every vector stores m bidirectional edges per node across graph layers, plus vertex metadata. IVFFlat stores only inverted list cluster centroids and vector lists, resulting in far smaller memory overhead at the cost of lower recall and QPS."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What maintenance_work_mem value is required to build a 1M vector HNSW index?",
